course: dictionary
lesson: 231
title: Alliance: working together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An alliance is an agreement between countries, groups or people to work together, or to help and protect each other. The sentence helps you: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy joined five, later six, nations in a lasting alliance.» Lasting means it went on for a long time, so an alliance is a deal that holds.
explain: Try the swap check. «By 1914 Europe's big powers were rivals in two alliances: Germany and Austria-Hungary on one side, and France, Russia and Britain on the other.» If you swap in "two groups that had agreed to help each other", the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: An alliance can also be the group that made the agreement. In the sentence above, the alliances are the two groups of countries. In a story, «characters form alliances to defeat a common enemy» means they agree to team up against the same enemy.
fact: An alliance is an agreement between countries, groups or people to work together or help and protect each other.
fact: «Alliance» can also mean the group of countries or people who have made that agreement.
fact: «Form an alliance» and «make an alliance» both mean to agree to join together.
fact: «Military alliance» means an alliance where members agree to defend each other if they are attacked, like NATO.
fact: «In alliance with» means working together with someone.
exercise: «By 1914 Europe's big powers were rivals in two alliances.» What is an alliance? | *An agreement to work together and help each other | A fight between two people | A large, old castle | A kind of weather
exercise: «Military alliance» suggests what? | A dinner party for leaders | *An agreement to defend each other if attacked | A school trip to the museum | A club for playing football
exercise: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy joined five, later six, nations in a lasting alliance.» What does lasting mean here? | *Going on for a long time | Secret and hidden | Short and quick | Loud and noisy
test: «Characters form alliances to defeat a common enemy.» What does form an alliance mean? | Run away from an enemy | Count to ten | *Agree to join together | Break a promise
test: Which word means a group of countries that have agreed to work together? | Army | Enemy | Rival | *Alliance
exam: Ella reads, «The teacher worked in alliance with the parents.» What does in alliance with mean? | Far away from | *Working together with | Copying | Against
